    <div class="primaryContent" role="main">
          <div id="mainContent">
              <!-- Page content -->
              
                            <h1>Computer Science Major - Bachelor of Computer and Information Sciences</h1>            <div class="row">
    <div class="col-lg-9 mainLeft"><div class="mb-small">
<div class="intro"><p>Study computer science and gain the skills to develop sophisticated software solutions, solve complex problems and use the power of computing technologies innovatively.</p></div>

<div id="content_container_82526_814206">
<p>Computer science is the study of how computers work and how they can help us solve complex problems and interact with the world around us. Computer scientists develop innovative solutions, improve existing technologies and drive technological advancements. This major is a mix of computing theory and practical implications to solve real-life problems; setting you up well for a wide range of careers that are in demand around the world.</p><p>
<div id="content_container_625438">
<div class="featuredPanel"><h2>Talk to us about your study options</h2><p>Thinking about studying at AUT? Book a time with us to discuss your study options.</p><p><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/meet-us-on-campus-to-discuss-your-options" class="btnLink">BOOK A SESSION</a></p></div>
</div>
</p>
</div>

<br><p>This is part of the <a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/engineering-computer-and-mathematical-sciences/courses/bachelor-of-computer-and-information-sciences">Bachelor of Computer and Information Sciences</a>.</p>
<!--<p class="mb3"><a class="goBackBtn" href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/engineering-computer-and-mathematical-sciences/courses/bachelor-of-computer-and-information-sciences"><span class="prev"><</span><span class="goBackText">Bachelor of Computer and Information Sciences</span></a></p>-->
<!--NOINDEX-->
<div class="progQuickBtn row">
  <div class="col-xs-6 col-sm-3"><a class="iconBtn open-popup-link" id="btnTab1" href="#brochure-popup" target="_blank">Brochure</a></div>
  <div class="col-xs-6 col-sm-3"><a class="iconBtn enquiry" data-cta-location='content' id="btnTab2" href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/enquiry/panel">Enquire</a></div>
    <div class="col-xs-6 col-sm-3"><a class="iconBtn" id="btnTab3" href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/applying">How to apply</a></div>
  <div class="col-xs-6 col-sm-3"><a class="iconBtn" data-cta-location='content' id="btnTab4" href="https://apply.aut.ac.nz?prog=AK3697" target="_blank">Apply now</a></div>
  </div>
<div id="brochure-popup" class="white-popup mfp-hide"><div class="container"><div class="whiteWraper">
    <style>.brochureItem{display: none;} .brochureItem[data-area*="A06"]{display: block;}</style>
<p class="b">Download programme guides</p><ul>
<li class="brochureItem" data-area="A06"><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/__data/assets/pdf_file/0003/1112439/2027-ECMS-web.pdf" target="_blank">Engineering, Computer and Maths (2027)</a></li>

<li class="brochureItem" data-area="A06"><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/__data/assets/pdf_file/0004/980005/ECMS-Final-Web.pdf" target="_blank">Engineering, Computer & Maths (2026)</a></li>
</ul>
    </div></div></div>

<!--ENDNOINDEX-->
<div id="content_container_2569_79568">
<!-- Template -  Start -->
<div id="tab"></div>
<link href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/__data/assets/css_file/0008/79577/tmp_tabbed-content.css" rel="stylesheet"/> <!-- .tmp_tabbed-content.css--> <!-- MOVE THIS TO THE DESIGN CSS FILE FOLDER -->
<div id="tmp_tabs-wrapper-814208" class="tmp_tabs-wrapper frontend">

            <div>
            
<div id="new_content_container_82528_814208">

</div>

        </div>
        
    <div class="responsiveTab uniTab" data-active="">
    
        <ul class="clearfix">
                <li class="active"><a href="#tab-814208-1" data-tabs="not-loaded"><span class="tableDiv"><span class="tableCell">What you study</span></span></a></li>
                            <li><a href="#tab-814208-2" data-tabs="not-loaded"><span class="tableDiv"><span class="tableCell">Career opportunities</span></span></a></li>
                                        <li><a href="#tab-814208-3" data-tabs="not-loaded"><span class="tableDiv"><span class="tableCell">Related programmes</span></span></a></li>
                                            </ul><!--.tmp_tabs-menu-->
        
        
                <div id="tab-814208-1" class="tab-pane active" data-content="1">
                    <p>The Computer Science major focuses on advanced programming, data structures, algorithm design, operating systems, computer graphics and artificial intelligence.</p><h2>Year 1</h2><p>You&rsquo;ll study six core courses that cover foundational computing knowledge, as well as a course on programming, covering the processes of program design and implementation using object-oriented programming.</p><h3>You study the following courses:</h3><h4>Core courses</h4><ul class="paperLinkList"><li>COMP500 Programming Concepts and Techniques</li><li>COMP501 Computing Technology in Society</li><li>COMP507 IT Project Management</li><li>COMP508 Database System Design</li><li>DIGD507 Collaborative Practices | Mahitahi</li><li>MATH503 Mathematics for Computing</li></ul><h4>Computer science course</h4><ul class="paperLinkList"><li>COMP503 Object Oriented Programming</li></ul><p>You also take the first course for your second major, minor or elective courses.</p><h2>Year 2</h2><p>Courses you study this year include data structures and algorithms, computer graphics programming, and logical and combinatorial tools and methods.</p><h3>You study the following courses:</h3><h4>Computer science courses</h4><ul class="paperLinkList"><li>COMP610 Data Structures and Algorithms</li><li>COMP611 Algorithm Design and Analysis</li><li>COMP612 Computer Graphics Programming</li><li>COMP613 Combinatorics and Graph Theory</li></ul><p>You also continue to take courses for your chosen second major, minor(s) or elective courses.</p><h2>Year 3</h2><p>Courses this year are related to computation theory, programming languages, and distributed and mobile systems.</p><h3>You study the following courses:</h3><h4>Computer science courses</h4><ul><li><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/rc/arion_address/paperdetails-refresh.php?paper_code=COMP711" target="_blank"> COMP711 Theory of Computation</a></li><li><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/rc/arion_address/paperdetails-refresh.php?paper_code=COMP712" target="_blank"> COMP712 Programming Languages</a></li><li>One of:<ul><li><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/rc/arion_address/paperdetails-refresh.php?paper_code=COMP713" target="_blank"> COMP713 Distributed and Mobile Systems</a></li><li><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/rc/arion_address/paperdetails-refresh.php?paper_code=COMP719" target="_blank">COMP719 Applied Human Computer Interaction</a></li></ul></li></ul><p>You also take the final courses for your chosen second major, minor(s) or elective courses.</p><h2>Study planner for this programme</h2><p>Download our study planner to see what your studies could look like in the Bachelor of Computer and Information Sciences.</p><p><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/__data/assets/pdf_file/0011/952796/BCIS-Programme-Structure-2026.pdf" target="_blank">Bachelor of Computer and Information Sciences study planner</a></p><h2>Workplace experience</h2><p>The Research and Development Project course in your final year brings together the skills you&rsquo;ve developed throughout your degree. You apply what you&rsquo;ve learnt throughout your studies in a project for an industry client or research centre, under the guidance of an experienced supervisor.</p><h3>Want more info about work integrated learning at AUT?</h3><p>Read more about workplace experience in AUT programmes, how it works and why it&rsquo;s so beneficial when you start your career.</p><p><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/workplace-experience-work-integrated-learning-in-aut-programmes">Workplace experience in AUT programmes</a></p><p>
<div id="component_945472">
<div class="oldP"><h2>Ready to enrol in your courses?</h2><p>Find out how you can enrol in the courses and classes for your programme, whether you&rsquo;ve just joined AUT as a new student or you&rsquo;re already studying with us. If you&rsquo;re looking for a course timetable or more info on a specific course <a aria-label="Link use our course search" id="menur5dg" href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/course-search" rel="noreferrer noopener">use our course search</a>.</p><p><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/student-life/studying/enrolling-in-courses-and-classes" class="btnLink">Enrol now</a></p></div><div class="newP" style="display:none;"><p class="b">Ready to enrol in your courses?</p><p>Find out how you can enrol in the courses and classes for your programme, whether you&rsquo;ve just joined AUT as a new student or you&rsquo;re already studying with us. If you&rsquo;re looking for a course timetable or more info on a specific course <a aria-label="Link use our course search" id="menur5dg" href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/course-search" rel="noreferrer noopener">use our course search</a>.</p><p><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/student-life/studying/enrolling-in-courses-and-classes">Enrol now</a></p></div>
</div>

<div id="component_1091296">
<script>
    $( document ).ready(function() {
    if (window.location.href.indexOf("?SQ_DESIGN_NAME=programme&SQ_PAINT_LAYOUT_NAME=new") > -1) {
    $('.oldP').hide();
    $('.newP').show();
    }
});
</script>
</div>
</p><div>
<div class="courseContent" id="content_container_728147">
<h2>Build your degree</h2><p>Use our online tool to build your own degree and see what your three years of study could look like.</p><p><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/degree-builder?prog=98499&amp;theme=orange" class="degreeBuildClick" target="_blank"><img src="https://www.aut.ac.nz/__data/assets/image/0007/1071268/BYD-content-banner-orange-780.png" class="degreeBuildImage" alt="Build your degree" /><img src="https://www.aut.ac.nz/__data/assets/image/0007/1071268/BYD-content-banner-orange-780.png" style="margin-bottom:30px;" class="degreeBuildMobile" alt="Build your degree" /><!-- Span bit is used for tracking and hidden. It enables GA to show link text. --><span class="degreeBuildPage">https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/engineering-computer-and-mathematical-sciences/courses/bachelor-of-computer-and-information-sciences/computer-science-major-bachelor-of-computer-and-information-sciences</span></a></p>
</div>
</div>
                    
                </div>
                            <div id="tab-814208-2" class="tab-pane" data-content="2">
                                                            <p>
<div id="component_1162946">
<p>The careers listed here are just some of the directions your studies could lead. Career titles can vary, but the skills behind them often connect. Explore our career finder to discover related careers, learn what they involve and view salary information.</p><p><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/career-finder?area=A06" class="btnLink btn btn-primary mb-3">Related careers</a></p><hr style="margin-bottom:30px;" />
</div>
</p><ul><li>Algorithm engineer</li><li>Back-end developer</li><li>Quantitative analyst/researcher</li><li>IT project manager</li></ul>
                                    </div>
                                        <div id="tab-814208-3" class="tab-pane" data-content="3">
                                     <h2>Other majors in the Bachelor of Computer and Information Sciences</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/engineering-computer-and-mathematical-sciences/courses/bachelor-of-computer-and-information-sciences/data-science-major-bachelor-of-computer-and-information-sciences">Data Science</a></li><li><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/engineering-computer-and-mathematical-sciences/courses/bachelor-of-computer-and-information-sciences/digital-services-major-bachelor-of-computer-and-information-sciences">Digital Services</a></li><li><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/engineering-computer-and-mathematical-sciences/courses/bachelor-of-computer-and-information-sciences/networks-and-cybersecurity-major-bachelor-of-computer-and-information-sciences">Networks and Cybersecurity</a></li><li><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/engineering-computer-and-mathematical-sciences/courses/bachelor-of-computer-and-information-sciences/software-development-major">Software Development</a></li></ul><h2>Postgraduate study</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/engineering-computer-and-mathematical-sciences/courses/postgraduate-certificate-in-computer-and-information-sciences">Postgraduate Certificate in Computer and Information Sciences</a></li><li><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/engineering-computer-and-mathematical-sciences/courses/postgraduate-diploma-in-computer-and-information-sciences">Postgraduate Diploma in Computer and Information Sciences</a></li><li><a href="https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/engineering-computer-and-mathematical-sciences/courses/master-of-computer-and-information-sciences">Master of Computer and Information Sciences</a></li></ul>
